|title=Well Tackled!
|chapter=17|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5387037W
|passage=Commander Birch was '''a trifle''' uneasy when he found there was more than a popple on the sea; it was, in fact, distinctly choppy. Strictly speaking, he ought to have been following up the picket–boat, but he was satisfied that the circumstances were sufficiently urgent for him to take risks.}}
#* '''1957''', {{w|Neville Shute}}, ''{{w|On the Beach (novel)|On the Beach}}'', New York: William Morrow, Chapter{{nbsp}}4,<sup>[https://www.fadedpage.com/books/20131214/html.php]</sup>
#*: He stared at the chart. “Maybe we’ll move away towards the west '''a trifle''', and come down on Fiji from the north.”
#* '''2006''', {{w|Ngũgĩ wa Thiong'o|Ngũgĩ wa Thiong’o}}, ''{{w|Wizard of the Crow}}'', New York: Knopf Doubleday, Book 3, p.{{nbsp}}411,<sup>[https://books.google.ca/books?id=k5snFSTVhOsC&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false]</sup>
#*: “Let’s get on with it,” Sikiokuu replied, '''a trifle''' impatiently.

